  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Placement is a dated observation",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: three AZs, six subnets; both node groups may use private A/B/C.",
        "OBSERVED on 29 October: three nodes A/A/C, two On-Demand and one Spot; RDS Single-AZ B. Subnet coverage is not workload HA.",
        "Private subnet boxes summarize placements, not fixed scheduling. Ingress and operator lanes below are logical paths within that topology."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "NAT data plane and recovery",
      "items": [
        "A NAT EC2 instance in each public subnet has an ENI, a stable EIP and SourceDestCheck disabled. Each private route table points to that ENI.",
        "ASG replaces an unhealthy member. EventBridge invokes Lambda; CONTROL/generation, ownership and per-slot journals guard EIP/route handoff.",
        "PROVEN: one replacement restored EIP and route in 178 seconds. UNVERIFIED: private egress after replacement, uninterrupted service and cross-AZ failover."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Access boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Management has no public IP or inbound SSH; its SSM Agent opens an outbound channel through NAT.",
        "An authorized Windows operator forwards loopback to the real private EKS or RDS hostname with full TLS verification.",
        "VPC Link → ALB port 80 → pod port 8080 is ingress. It does not traverse a NAT instance. EKS/management PostgreSQL SG access was removed during cost-down."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and current state",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: arrows describe source-backed design; the reading guide gives the source for each relationship.",
        "OBSERVED: topology captured on 28–29 October 2026. Runtime retired on 29 October; RDS retained stopped.",
        "PROVEN applies only to named experiments. These diagrams are not live telemetry or a production certification."
      ]
    }
  ],
